<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Manuel Balmaceda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1840">1840</a>–<a href="/years/1891">1891</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Manuel Balmaceda was president of Chile from 1886 to 1891. He used nitrate revenue for public works, but his conflict with Congress over the budget led to the civil war of 1891, in which the navy and Congress defeated the army loyal to him. After his defeat he took refuge in the Argentine legation and shot himself at the end of his term.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the civil war of 1891, in which Congress defeated President <b>José Manuel Balmaceda</b>, the period known as the Parliamentary Republic followed, until the Constitution of 1925 restored presidential power.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Republic of Chile · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Chile saw nearly sixty years of orderly presidential successions under its constitution of 1833, until a conflict between President <b>José Manuel Balmaceda</b> and Congress ended in civil war in 1891, and Costa Rica, which abolished its army in 1948–1949, has elected its presidents without interruption since then.</blockquote><a href="/government/presidential-democracy">Presidential democracy · Through History</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Bucalemu, in what is now <a href="/countries/chile">Chile</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/chile">Chile</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=-34.64,-72.04&amp;year=1873" aria-label="Bucalemu on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2720 3418 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of José Manuel Balmaceda"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3170 3688h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3170 3688h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=-34.64,-72.04&amp;year=1873">What was here in 1873? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
